Subject: Cantor Accountable Basket Attention Stress Evaluation Design

@ [evaluation_design_uuid] f76ce32a-e1a7-4b9b-8fa1-339057be7adf
@ [conversation_uuid] 8fac2e83-9ba0-4c02-af5e-6a9e6f1dce24
@ [design_date] 2026-09-01
@ [P6_implementation_map_commit] 180bef70b80bd4f09f70ae75dd2832811d6a9661

& [Purpose]
  + measure whether explicit identity accounting improves an inference model's observable ability to individuate track refresh and correctly reference a basket of same-type objects

& [PrimaryHypothesis]
  + stable exact handles plus a complete manifest selective materialization and full-coverage receipt reduce identity swaps false merges silent omissions stale references and invented members relative to prose-only context

& [Treatments]
  + [T0_prose] natural-language object descriptions with no structured handles
  + [T1_handles] the same descriptions with stable exact handles embedded in prose
  + [T2_full_register] current complete full-object AccountabilityInferenceWindow
  + [T3_manifest] proposed complete compact manifest with exact materialization on demand
  + [T4_manifest_receipt] manifest and materialization followed by required member-by-member attention receipt
  + [T5_host_checked] T4 with every resolution read and mutation routed through the current or P6 Cantor host protocol

& [IndependentAxes]
  + basket size is 2 4 8 16 32 64 and capacity-permitting 128
  + type collision is distinct types shared type shared type plus overlapping labels and deliberately identical display labels
  + differentiator sparsity is obvious subtle temporally changing and absent-until-queried
  + reference form is exact handle unique label ambiguous label definite noun phrase pronoun ordinal and prior-state description
  + distractor distance is immediate short medium long and near-context-limit
  + update pressure is none one object patch interleaved patches admission after initial frame and stale replay attempt
  + task pressure is lookup comparison ordering planning constraint satisfaction and proposed mutation
  + sampling condition records model version reasoning effort temperature seed when available and complete prompt/output bytes

& [BlindedCaseConstruction]
  + a deterministic generator creates objects answer keys and prompt variants from one case seed
  + surface names are randomized independently of handles so semantic familiarity cannot reveal the answer
  + collision cases deliberately reuse types labels roles and purposes while preserving one hidden differentiator
  + mutation cases preserve every generation and ask questions that distinguish current from predecessor state
  + the evaluator receives exact expected handles states generations and permitted Unknown or Ambiguous results but the model does not receive the answer key

& [CoreTasks]
  + enumerate every member exactly once
  + resolve each reference or explicitly return Ambiguous or Unknown
  + answer state questions by exact handle after distractor passages
  + compare two same-type members without importing a third member's attributes
  + apply a proposed change to the named member and report every unchanged member
  + reject a stale update after an intervening generation
  + identify newly admitted identity without merging it into its nearest same-type neighbor
  + produce a full disposition receipt and hold when a material member remains unresolved

& [FailureTaxonomy]
  + identity_swap attributes or action move from intended handle to another existing handle
  + false_merge two handles are treated as one object
  + false_split one handle is invented as multiple objects
  + silent_omission an existing manifest member disappears from required accounting
  + invented_member output names an unprovided handle or entity as present
  + ambiguity_collapse a genuinely ambiguous reference is guessed as exact
  + stale_dereference predecessor state is reported as current after refresh
  + collateral_mutation a non-target member changes
  + unresolved_laundering missing information becomes confident NotApplicable or a factual claim
  + protocol_bypass model answers or mutates despite a typed host refusal

& [Metrics]
  + exact member recall precision and recall
  + exact reference resolution accuracy with separate Ambiguous and Unknown calibration
  + per-task identity swap false merge omission invention stale and collateral rates
  + complete-receipt rate held-when-required rate and unjustified NotApplicable rate
  + successful task rate conditional on protocol acceptance
  + tokens bytes latency and host calls per correct result
  + error rate as a function of basket size collision distractor distance and update generation

& [Comparisons]
  + T0 versus T1 isolates the value of stable textual handles
  + T1 versus T2 isolates complete structured roster and full state injection
  + T2 versus T3 tests whether compact manifest plus selective detail preserves accuracy while extending capacity
  + T3 versus T4 isolates whether explicit attention accounting improves behavioral consistency
  + T4 versus T5 isolates host enforcement from model self-report

& [Controls]
  + all treatments receive semantically equal source facts and task order for a case
  + treatment formatting and token counts are recorded and a length-matched distractor control distinguishes structure from extra repetition
  + exact deterministic host outcomes are scored separately from model prose quality
  + order is counterbalanced and model conversations are isolated to prevent cross-case memory
  + evaluator logic is deterministic and independently tested before any model comparison

& [ExpectedFalsifiers]
  + if T1 performs like T0 stable handles alone do not create reliable behavioral pointers
  + if T3 degrades sharply from T2 materialization selection is hiding required state or manifest cues are too weak
  + if T4 does not improve T3 the receipt may be bureaucratic output rather than an effective attention operation
  + if T5 improves correctness only by refusing most work report acceptance-conditioned and total utility rather than declaring success
  + if errors remain dominated by long-range distractors even under T5 the host needs stronger refresh cadence or task decomposition not activation mysticism

& [FirstMinimumRun]
  + use basket sizes 2 8 and 32 with shared type overlapping labels one patch and one stale attempt
  + run T0 T1 T2 and after P6 T3 T4 T5 over at least twenty deterministic cases per cell
  + pre-register metrics thresholds and preserve every input output model setting host event and scorer result
  + inspect failures qualitatively only after aggregate scoring is sealed

& [ConnectionToAttentionEngineering]
  + success means the engineered context and host protocol produce fewer observable identity failures under controlled pressure
  + the experiment does not claim to reveal transformer attention weights private chain of thought subjective awareness or literal pointer structures
  + a receipt is tested as a behavioral intervention and accountability proof not accepted as evidence that the model internally attended

& [Nonclaims]
  + no model execution dataset result threshold or empirical advantage exists yet
  + this design is not an authorization to spend external API credits or publish results
  + hallucination intuition and dream-walking claims require separate evaluations after identity tracking is established

& [RecommendedNext]
  + implement P6 then build the deterministic case generator scorer and T0 through T5 runner as a separately signed evaluation slice
